{"name":"Spa Retreat","hex":"#d4e4e6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Spanish."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A health resort near a mineral spring or hot spring.","A trendy or fashionable resort."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spa"},{"term":"retreat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of pulling back or withdrawing, as from something dangerous, or unpleasant.\n\nThe act of reversing direction and receding from a forward position.\n Withdrawal by a military force from a dangerous position or from enemy attack.","The act of reversing direction and receding from a forward position."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To withdraw from a position, go back.\n To withdraw military forces.","To withdraw military forces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retreat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Retreat (spiritual)","blocks":[{"text":"The meaning of a spiritual retreat can be different for different religious communities. Spiritual retreats are an integral part of many Buddhist, Christian and Sufi communities. There are many different types of spiritual retreats such as wellness retreats, mindfulness retreats, spa retreats, adventure retreats, detox retreats, yoga retreats, and religious retreats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/000000000_WinShape.jpg/330px-000000000_WinShape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retreat_(spiritual)","wikidata":"Q19299086"},{"title":"Spa","blocks":[{"text":"A spa is a location where mineral-rich spring water is used to give medicinal baths. Spa health treatments are known as balneotherapy. The belief in the curative powers of mineral waters and hot springs goes back to prehistoric times. Spa towns, spa resorts, and day spas are popular worldwide, but are especially widespread in Europe and Japan. Bathing regimens in ancient Greece formed the foundation for modern spa procedures. Following a decline in public bathing during medieval times, spas became popular health resorts and social centers for the upper class in the 18th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Medicinal_spa_of_Hark%C3%A1ny.jpg/330px-Medicinal_spa_of_Hark%C3%A1ny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spa","wikidata":"Q1341387"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/BJ23-chapel.jpg/500px-BJ23-chapel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/BJ23-chapel.jpg/1280px-BJ23-chapel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/BJ23-chapel.jpg/500px-BJ23-chapel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An aspiring seminarian prays during a vocational discernment retreat in the chapel of Blessed John XXIII National Seminary in Massachusetts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABJ23-chapel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Young_monk_in_meditation_cell%2C_Yerpa%2C_Tibet._1993.jpg/500px-Young_monk_in_meditation_cell%2C_Yerpa%2C_Tibet._1993.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Young_monk_in_meditation_cell%2C_Yerpa%2C_Tibet._1993.jpg/500px-Young_monk_in_meditation_cell%2C_Yerpa%2C_Tibet._1993.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young monk in meditation retreat, Yerpa, Tibet in 1993","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYoung_monk_in_meditation_cell%2C_Yerpa%2C_Tibet._1993.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thum